### Deedify Backend API Testing
### Base URL: http://localhost:3001/api

### 1. Create a new order (PENDING status)
POST http://localhost:3001/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "user123",
  "listingId": "listing456",
  "quantity": 10,
  "paymentMethod": "FIAT"
}

### 2. Simulate fiat payment success (triggers escrow release + token minting)
POST http://localhost:3001/api/orders/fiat/webhook
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "{{orderId}}",
  "status": "success",
  "paymentId": "stripe_payment_123",
  "transactionId": "tx_456",
  "amount": 5000
}

### 3. Simulate fiat payment failure
POST http://localhost:3001/api/orders/fiat/webhook
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "{{orderId}}",
  "status": "failed",
  "paymentId": "stripe_payment_124"
}

### 4. Get order by ID
GET http://localhost:3001/api/orders/{{orderId}}

### 5. Get user's orders
GET http://localhost:3001/api/orders/user/user123

### 6. Get all orders (admin)
GET http://localhost:3001/api/orders

### ========================================
### EXAMPLE WORKFLOW (Copy orderId from step 1 response)
### ========================================

### Step 1: Create test data first (you'll need to run Prisma migrations and seed)
### Then create an order:
POST http://localhost:3001/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "test-user-1",
  "listingId": "test-listing-1",
  "quantity": 5,
  "paymentMethod": "FIAT"
}

### Step 2: Copy the order ID from above response and use it here:
### Replace "ORDER_ID_HERE" with actual order ID
POST http://localhost:3001/api/orders/fiat/webhook
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORDER_ID_HERE",
  "status": "success",
  "paymentId": "test_payment_123",
  "transactionId": "test_tx_456",
  "amount": 2500
}

### Step 3: Check the completed order:
GET http://localhost:3001/api/orders/ORDER_ID_HERE

### ========================================
### HEALTH CHECK
### ========================================

### Simple health check - should return empty array initially
GET http://localhost:3001/api/orders